@@s001 Python for the exercises
@@s002 dato:element of a,due:element of b,ok:accumulated sum
@@s003 Two lists of the same length. <code>somma</code> starts from 0.
@@s004 <code>zip</code> takes the elements in position 0: the pair (2, 3). <code>x, y</code> unpacks it: x = 2, y = 3.
@@s005 <code>somma += x * y</code>: 0 + 2·3 = <b>6</b>.
@@s006 Position 1: the pair (2, 4).
@@s007 6 + 2·4 = <b>14</b>. The pairs are finished: the loop stops and the function returns 14.
